/*****************************************************************************
    limitT -- the control for fixIts F-27, Tony's ruling of 2026-08-19: a write
    to maxLimit that yields a zero or non numeric count is refused AT THE WRITE,
    and the assignment does not take.

    THE ROWS ARE ORDERED SO THAT RETAINED IS DISTINGUISHABLE FROM NEVER CHANGED.
    Row 2 moves the limit to a value nothing else in the system would produce,
    so when row 3 and row 4 are refused, the value that survives is provably the
    one row 2 put there rather than the boot default. A refusal test that ran
    only against the boot value could not tell a working refusal from a write
    that never happened.

    ROW 2 IS ALSO THE NEGATIVE CONTROL, per rule H7. It is a legitimate re pin
    and it must be SILENT. If every write reported, rows 3 and 4 would go green
    on an instrument that simply always fires.

    Row 4 is the sharper of the two refusals. A string leaves the count reading
    LARGE rather than zero, because getCount hands back the union field for an
    isSTRING and that overlaps the text pointer, so a count only test would wave
    it through. Row 3 is the plain zero.

    SENTINEL AT THE FOOT, and one stop only.
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(unitTests);
search reset stack Grokking;
search UnitTests list;
register(LimitTest);
define
    runLimit code={
        print "1 boot default:";
        print + "   maxLimit = " maxLimit:;
        print "2 legitimate re-pin to 250 -- MUST BE SILENT:";
        maxLimit = 250;
        print + "   maxLimit = " maxLimit:;
        print "3 refused write of zero -- reports, and 250 must survive:";
        maxLimit = 0;
        print + "   maxLimit = " maxLimit:;
        print "4 refused write of a string -- reports, and 250 must survive:";
        maxLimit = "big";
        print + "   maxLimit = " maxLimit:;
        print "5 legitimate re-pin still works after two refusals:";
        maxLimit = 300;
        print + "   maxLimit = " maxLimit:;
        };
    ;
runLimit();
print "LT SENTINEL":;
stop();
